Subject: [PATCH] docs(browser): document managed Chrome opt-in configuration
 [daveey]

---
 website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md b/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
index 528b113e1d..12a3308eba 100644
--- a/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
+++ b/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
@@ -2780,6 +2780,8 @@ browser:
     adopt_existing_tab: false    # Reuse an existing tab for this identity before creating one
 ```
 
+Managed Chrome is an experimental, explicit opt-in. Set `browser.managed_agent.endpoint` to the same exact loopback HTTP root as `browser.cdp_url` and set `browser.managed_agent.installation_id` to the identity generated by the managed supervisor installation. Both default to an empty string (disabled). A deliberately stopped supervisor requires explicit operator activation; core never infers management from a port or bootstraps a disabled service.
+
 **Dialog policies:**
 
 - `must_respond` (default) — capture the dialog, surface it in `browser_snapshot.pending_dialogs`, and wait for the agent to call `browser_dialog(action=...)`. After `dialog_timeout_s` seconds with no response, the dialog is auto-dismissed to prevent the page's JS thread from stalling forever.
